Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Gravitational corrections to matter propagators", "Title",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"b1870694-48db-4d3b-a510-3651c3d5bcda"],

Cell["\<\
Explore the graviton contributions to scalar, fermion, massive-vector, \
massless-vector, gluon and quark two-point functions. Follow one sector at a \
time to learn vertex assembly, loop reduction and result inspection.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"1a8a7cfe-8200-4a31-b209-fb4fb5d419c3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"faffbe22-3228-4446-8054-da7dcb431001"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"1273878a-8bc7-432d-9193-63868c6c4479"],

Cell["\<\
Saved outputs are retained from the previous evaluation. Bubble calculations \
and their displayed comparisons have not been rerun as part of this notebook \
revision. Reevaluate dependent cells to obtain results for the current inputs.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"9b796ff5-92fd-462c-a4df-ddcadaed6275"],

